3729-Provider Protocol 3.0.0 binds Structured Error 1.3.0. A syntactically valid v3
3730-request receives the v3 envelope with Error 1.3 on failure. A v2/v3 major
3731-mismatch, an unparseable or oversize first frame, or output that cannot be
3732:framed follows the Section 15.1 close/termination rule; the caller never trusts
3733-a different major's error. A dual-stack adapter advertises and validates v2 and
3734-v3 independently. It MAY translate only <code>ax.tmux</code> and
3735-<code>ax.conpty</code> to the immutable v2 descriptor under Section 4.E; every
3736-other backend is <code>incompatible_protocol</code>, not a fallback.
